23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span><span class="baseClass RatingStar--small"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation"><path class="RatingStar__fill" d="M24 9.63469C24 9.35683 23.7747 9.13158 23.4969 9.13158H15.0892L12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8590298927">May 10, 2026</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted"><br />I did a really stupid thing, I started reading this book just before 10pm, do not make the same mistake, you won't be able to sleep until you've read it to the end....This entire series wrapped me up in a cosy, whimsical blanket I didn't want to relinquish. This author's writing style is so uniquely...may I use the word adorable? Because, yes, every book she writes IS adorable, her characters are adorable, the world she plonks me in is adorable and, like the previous books in this series, I just wanted to hug the book, the characters, the author! Ms Morgan imbues me with such joy each time I read any of her books, I'm ready to do a happy dance when I finish! But now to the why she has this effect on me...<br /><br />Bastian Blackbriar is reneging on his duties, according to his quite vocal mother that is. By now, he's supposed to be, at the very least, betrothed, if not married. But he's not in a hurry, he's young, he wants to enjoy life before committing. However, mother dearest reminds him that he HAS to court a certain young lady, Lady Aveline Thornhart, who, as it so happens, is attending a prestigious event held by a prestigious family. The Thornhart's themselves are prestigious and their magic is what his mother covets; the raw magic that the Thornhart's possess. Not in an evil manner, she takes the responsibility of keeping the magic lines powerful all too seriously. <br /><br />Although Bastian's cousin, Hadrian tells him, “Not all of us consider commitment a terminal illness.” Bastian sees a noose around his head and his ankle and his wrists, an unbreakable shackle he would avoid at all costs. For now. Mama has an agenda to strengthen their family name and their magic, thus elevating them in society. But comply he will, on his terms. And that, to him, meant sabotage from the onset. The lady in question, Aveline, is in a conundrum of her own. After her disastrous coming out last season, her strong-willed grandma is pushing her to be courted by Jasvisn, grandson of her greatest rival/friend. Yes, Lady Aramind and Lady Rivienna, were friends, ARE friends, just have a friendly competition going on, kinda... I'd almost forgotten HOW much I adore Lady Rivienna, and loved her even more as she offered extremely sage advice later on in the book. The appearance of Bastian and Hadrian puts paid to that scheme except, now the meticulously banter takes centre stage, with Bastian poking at all of Aveline's insecurities, riling her up, and she trying to be the epitome of decorum and proprietary.<br /><br />The banter right off the bat was hilarious, Bastian not holding back one iota, much to the dismay of Hadrian, sees right through Aveline's carefully crafted words and promptly asks, "forgive me—do you have any opinions that haven’t been pre-approved for polite company, or shall I simply consult the manual?” Aveline HAD been trained to be as amenable as possible, bland, and respectful. Her opinions were of little matter, what mattered was that she present herself with no visible emotions, to be conversational, to be a lady offering the "correct" answers. Rather dull indeed. Something Aveline detested doing and Bastian's preconceived opinion, solidly confirmed. These are so different, yet so alike. He's flamboyant, he's a flirt, he rarely takes anything seriously and his easy charm could melt an iceberg. He hides behind a huge wall, a facade firmly erected, one no one can shatter, where he nurses his feelings of inadequacy, his feelings of unworthiness. She, distraught at the events from her coming out, hides behind her wall of brainless, emotionless facade. Neither of them is truly what they present. Ms Morgan's conveying it all is exemplary. <br /><br />I can't express how much I loved these characters! How much I loved this book! But my word, I wanted to box Bastian's ears when he provoced Aveline, nudging her with his amplifying magic, when she could barely contain it! And his baiting continues, until his guilt prompts him to end it. But another scheme is lurking in Bastian's head and this time, I wanted to smack my lips to his forehead and hug him! Rachel spun all of this immaculately, from the feelings of despair exuding from both Bastian and Aveline, to the utter delight I had, at THEIR utter delight and achieving a cease fire, a mutually beneficial one. My mouth curled into a smile and stayed there, getting bigger and bigger with each passing antic and I was infused with warmth from my head right down to my toes. I loved both these characters from incept but very quickly got to adore them. Ms Morgan gave me the whole enchilada, nuanced, painted with care, she draw their personalities meticulously. He, with his amplifying magic, is always the bridesmaid, never the bride, or I should say, always the bestman, never the groom. His magic makes everyone shine, he's pretty invisible. She, exhausted by containing her magic, a magic so uncontrolled if let loose, calls to her, constantly. Heck, just thinking about it I'm exhausted for Aveline! <br /><br />Finally, finally, able to take a breather, Aveline's relief was like a balm on my own soul. The banter was brilliance personified, from the entire cast of characters but it was the verbal rallies Aveline and Bastian had which made me giggle. I was so vested in them, probably more than is healthy but I blame the author for giving them such panache, making them 2 characters who tugged at my heart, made me smile, had me laughing out loud. Bastian changed tactics and slowly coaxed the hidden Aveline to appear and she *gasp* started having fun! Their... understanding... becomes comfortable, then it evolves to a genuine pleasurable experience, except, this was not what was expected from Aveline. Just seeing their emotions surfacing, trying to suppress them, made me want to howl at the injustice! <br /><br />There's the most adorable frost pixie who is very opinionated, she has followed Bastian and gives him a run for his money! Her messages on windows, just hilarious! And it takes this tiny tot to get Bastian to acknowledge certain truths. Oh, and Hadrian made me snort laugh with his questioning Aveline about her gloves and about a book she was raving about...you HAVE to read this book to understand why... yet again, a stroke or genius by the author. As for Hadrian, HE is pure joy! His mere presence in this book was heavenly! And you know what else Rachel does to perfection? Miscommunication, the assumptions of her characters, of what they perceive as truth, is so plausible it dupes me, nevermind the characters themselves. The romance is toe curlingly awesome, super clean but she still captures all the yearning, all the angst, all the feels, so much so, the butterflies in my stomach just couldn't settle! The HEA couldn't be more beautiful if an enhancing spell had been cast, although, Ms Morgan must possess loads of magic within her to make me devour every book she writes! Loved it? Heck no! I ADORED this book! <br /><br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">1 like</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 L6,19 C4.8954305,19 4,18.1045695 4,17 L4,12 C4,10.8954305 4.8954305,10 6,10 L8,10 C8.60249245,10 9.14276174,10.2664091 9.50943372,10.6878531 L9.58578644,10.6036344 L11,9.18942086 L11,6.75238209 C10.9999468,5.91477784 11.5910613,5.1935667