All 4 of these Charmed Leaf Legacy books I have read have left me feeling seen in some capacity - each character has something they struggle with, and it always strikes a chord for me. This story - a novella really - strikes the nail on the head again. <br /><br />Frost &amp; Fae Bargains is a forced proximity romance following side characters that are briefly mentioned in the main series, Aveline Thornhart and Bastian Blackbriar. Their story is our first non-Rowanwood romance set within this world, and it’s just as good as the main series. Morgan does a great job at fleshing out the winter traditions of the higher echelons of Fae Society, and crafts a delightfully cozy winter read that glitters like snow. <br /><br />I really appreciate how Bastian and Aveline’s struggles are very nearly mirrors of each other: he, the disappointing second son who is never good enough, and Aveline, who is made to stifle her real personality as much as possible. Both of them hide behinds facades, and it is the slow melting of their masks that makes this story so well plotted and engaging to read. You truly end up rooting for both of them, because it is so clear that they are drawn to each other like magnets because of how much they are kindred spirits. <br /><br />Something I have appreciated about this series is how extremely character driven it is, owing to the fact that there is never real high stakes. It’s a cozy regency inspired setting, and as such the characters have to be the driving force for the narrative to be engaging. This is Rachel Morgan’s greatest strength. Her dialogue craft is excellent - she’s very good with banter and chemistry and it’s something I always look forward to with this series. <br /><br />That said, something I would like to see with the remaining Charmed Leaf Legacy titles we are to receive later this year is perhaps a little bit more world building. I adore this series; I have loved every single title I have read within it. I want to know more about this world we get snatched glimpses of more and more with every book, so I am hoping Kazrian and Rosavyn’s stories deliver in this regard. <br /><br />This series has shaped up to be one of my favorite indie series I have read, and I highly recommend it for those readers who want a change of pace with a swoony-not-spicy romance. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25833456?shelf=fantasy-sci-fi" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fantasy-sci-fi</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25833456?shelf=favorites" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">favorites</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 