my goodness, another winner for Rachel. The love I have for the series is SO much. I love the world and the characters she’s created. This was such a fun surprise book &amp; I loved going back in time a bit and seeing some of our beloved characters before they met their match. 🥹 <br /><br />I was captivated quickly by the story between Bastian &amp; Aveline. Rachel once again writes the most delicious tension and swoon that will give you one million butterflies and you’ll be soaking up every single moment! I was giggling and kicking my feet over subtle looks &amp; hand brushes 🤭<br /><br />Bastian has this carefree attitude about him, but you could also tell very quickly that there was more beneath it. Aveline was the most prim &amp; proper, until she met Bastian and slipped and showed her true colors (pun intended!), which intrigued Bastian! <br /><br />The story woven throughout this was filled with hope &amp; accepting who you are and being yourself wholly &amp; completely. Bastian saw through the facade that Aveline had up and saw her tenacity &amp; competitive side, and he often pushed her to show that side of herself. He showed her there was nothing wrong with who she was. I loved watching him help her believe it! And how he helped her with her magic?! Doing it anytime she needed &amp; doing it without even thinking. He was just always aware of her needs, and always listening.<br /><br />And she did the same for Bastian. He often felt second best, but she showed him he wasn’t. That he had just as much to offer as any other eligible man. That his magic wasn’t just to boast others up, that it could truly help others! <br /><br />And Aveline’s Magic?! It sounded so beautiful. I could picture it so vividly in my head. I felt like I was transported to another world as she’d describe it! <br /><br />Ok this is the longest review ever, but I just loved this book SO much!! <br /></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tag