sts and Tea Leaves.) It was a grand time just like all the books leading up to this one! I loved the whimsical christmas festivities vibe in this one... very cozy and lots of vivid detail/a fun read! This one spoke to me personally as I have struggles similar to both the FMC and MMC in feeling either not enough or too much simultaneously. There was a little side kick frost faerie in the story and she is spunky, hilarious, attentive, and everything a fun side kick should be! I love that the book ended with the FMC and her grandmother finding mutual ground and healing in thier differences. As always the romance was divine. We start out as mutual enemies to lovers turned partners in crime driving each other mad but by the end they are full of yearning, swoon worthy pining, and sweet touches of affection/kisses only. A 1 on my SPICE SCALE🌶️, because while there was absolutely 0 spice or language, there is detailed descriptions (in the end of the book in one scene) of desire and what it's making them feel. Rachel has done it again!! **To read this free copy latest installment of The Charmed Leaf series, go to Rachel's website now and sign up for her newsletter! She'll send you an email with links to all her bonus content as this is a standalone bonus story. ** #charmedleafseries #faeregencyromantasy #rachelmorganreads #whimsicalwinterreads #frostandfaebargains happy reading!! LINK: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" href="https://join.rachel-morgan.com/frost">https://join.rachel-morgan.com/frost</a></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Ico