id="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">-He falls first<br />-Funny pixie sidekicks<br />-Winter, cozy vibes<br />-Growing in self-worth<br />-SWOONY spice-free romance <br /><br />Squealing. Kicking my feet.<br />The TENSION in this one!! Holy cow, who knew painting could be so intimate and romantic. BUT completely spice-free! But still packed full of swoon and tension. <br /><br />Rachel is truly one of the best writers I have stumbled upon in a long time. So many of her lines are quotable, memorable, and full of wit. She is a phenomenal writer of banter and spice-free romance. But she nails the whimsy and humor side as well. <br /><br />Just like with Aurelise, I really connected with Aveline. As someone who has been told they are "too much," her story resonated with me. I was cheering her to stand her ground and be who she really is from the beginning. <br />Bastian was once again a great MC. He falls first is quickly becoming one of my favorite tropes. He loved her so tenderly and so unabashedly. Rachel is once again making it impossible for a real man to ever measure up! :)</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/161300758?shelf=2026-reads" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">2026-reads</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.14442