or":{"__ref":"User:147181181"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1783701882647,"createdAt":1783378180859,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1783378197333,"text":"I’m glad what was supposed to be a short side story spiralled into this. The world of the Charmed Leaf Legacy books is such a sweet and cozy one. The wintry setting added a fun new element, and it was interesting to see some of the main characters before their stories began. I really enjoyed Ava and Bastian as main characters. I wish we had been able to see more of what Bastian was able to do with his magic after finding more purpose/confidence in himself. However, since this wasn’t originally intended to be a full book, I can understand why that wasn’t included. \u003cbr /\u003e","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3T5B99MUDQTBS\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:46049572":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":46049572,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1767078922i/46049572._UX200_CR0,36,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":130,"textReviewsCount":1685,"name":"Beba Andric","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/46049572-beba-andric","contributor":null,"id":46049572},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A194A75Y5I1DW2":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A194A75Y5I1DW2"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A194A75Y5I1DW2\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A194A75Y5I1DW2","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A194A75Y5I1DW2"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/46049572?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8590298927"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2026051016.698ea65a-f12c-4c11-819d-e55111f473bb":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2026051016.698ea65a-f12c-4c11-819d-e55111f473bb","creator":{"__ref":"User:46049572"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778429857005,"createdAt":1778429833106,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1778429856828,"text":"\u003cbr /\u003eI did a really stupid thing, I started reading this book just before 10pm, do not make the same mistake, you won't be able to sleep until you've read it to the end....This entire series wrapped me up in a cosy, whimsical blanket I didn't want to relinquish. This author's writing style is so uniquely...may I use the word adorable? Because, yes, every book she writes IS adorable, her characters are adorable, the world she plonks me in is adorable and, like the previous books in this series, I just wanted to hug the book, the characters, the author! Ms Morgan imbues me with such joy each time I read any of her books, I'm ready to do a happy dance when I finish! But now to the why she has this effect on me...\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBastian Blackbriar is reneging on his duties, according to his quite vocal mother that is. By now, he's supposed to be, at the very least, betrothed, if not married. But he's not in a hurry, he's young, he wants to enjoy life before committing. However, mother dearest reminds him that he HAS to court a certain young lady, Lady Aveline Thornhart, who, as it so happens, is attending a prestigious event held by a prestigious family. The Thornhart's themselves are prestigious and their magic is what his mother covets; the raw magic that the Thornhart's possess. Not in an evil manner, she takes the responsibility of keeping the magic lines powerful all too seriously. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlthough Bastian's cousin, Hadrian tells him, “Not all of us consider commitment a terminal illness.” Bastian sees a noose around his head and his ankle and his wrists, an unbreakable shackle he would avoid at all costs. For now. Mama has an agenda to strengthen their family name and their magic, thus elevating them in society. But comply he will, on his terms. And that, to him, meant sabotage from the onset. The lady in question, Aveline, is in a conundrum of her own. After her disastrous coming out last season, her strong-willed grandma is pushing her to be courted by Jasvisn, grandson of her greatest rival/friend. Yes, Lady Aramind and Lady Rivienna, were friends, ARE friends, just have a friendly competition going on, kinda... I'd almost forgotten HOW much I adore Lady Rivienna, and loved her even more as she offered extremely sage advice later on in the book. The appearance of Bastian and Hadrian puts paid to that scheme except, now the meticulously banter takes centre stage, with Bastian poking at all of Aveline's insecurities, riling her up, and she trying to be the epitome of decorum and proprietary.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe banter right off the bat was hilarious, Bastian not holding back one iota, much to the dismay of Hadrian, sees right through Aveline's carefully crafted words and promptly asks, \"forgive me—do you have any opinions that haven’t been pre-approved for polite company, or shall I simply consult the manual?” Aveline HAD been trained to be as amenable as possible, bland, and respectful. Her opinions were of little matter, what mattered was that she present herself with no visible emotions, to be conversational, to be a lady offering the \"correct\" answers. Rather dull indeed. Something Aveline detested doing and Bastian's preconceived opinion, solidly confirmed. These are so different, yet so alike. He's flamboyant, he's a flirt, he rarely takes anything seriously and his easy charm could melt an iceberg. He hides behind a huge wall, a facade firmly erected, one no one can shatter, where he nurses his feelings of inadequacy, his feelings of unworthiness. She, distraught at the events from her coming out, hides behind her wall of brainless, emotionless facade. Neither of them is truly what they present. Ms Morgan's conveying it all is exemplary. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI can't express how much I loved these characters! How much I loved this book! But my word, I wanted to box Bastian's ears when he provoced Aveline, nudging her with his amplifying magic, when she could barely contain it! And his baiting continues, until his guilt prompts him to end it. But another scheme is lurking in Bastian's head and this time, I wanted to smack my lips to his forehead and hug him! Rachel spun all of this immaculately, from the feelings of despair exuding from both Bastian and Aveline, to the utter delight I had, at THEIR utter delight and achieving a cease fire, a mutually beneficial one. My mouth curled into a smile and stayed there, getting bigger and bigger with each passing antic and I was infused with warmth from my head right down to my toes. I loved both these characters from incept but very quickly got to adore them. Ms Morgan gave me the whole enchilada, nuanced, painted with care, she draw their personalities meticulously. He, with his amplifying magic, is always the bridesmaid, never the bride, or I should say, always the bestman, never the groom. His magic makes everyone shine, he's pretty invisible. She, exhausted by containing her magic, a magic so uncontrolled if let loose, calls to her, constantly. Heck, just thinking about it I'm exhausted for Aveline! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFinally, finally, able to take a breather, Aveline's relief was like a balm on my own soul. The banter was brilliance personified, from the entire cast of characters but it was the verbal rallies Aveline and Bastian had which made me giggle. I was so vested in them, probably more than is healthy but I blame the author for giving them such panache, making them 2 characters who tugged at my heart, made me smile, had me laughing out loud. Bastian changed tactics and slowly coaxed the hidden Aveline to appear and she *gasp* started having fun! Their... understanding... becomes comfortable, then it evolves to a genuine pleasurable experience, except, this was not what was expected from Aveline. Just seeing their emotions surfacing, trying to suppress them, made me want to howl at the injustice! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThere's the most adorable frost pixie who is very opinionated, she has followed Bastian and gives him a run for his money! Her messages on windows, just hilarious! And it takes this tiny tot to get Bastian to acknowledge certain truths. Oh, and Hadrian made me snort laugh with his questioning Aveline about her gloves and about a book she was raving about...you HAVE to read this book to understand why... yet again, a stroke or genius by the author. As for Hadrian, HE is pure joy! His mere presence in this book was heavenly! And you know what else Rachel does to perfection? Miscommunication, the assumptions of her characters, of what they perceive as truth, is so plausible it dupes me, nevermind the characters themselves. The romance is toe curlingly awesome, super clean but she still captures all the yearning, all the angst, all the feels, so much so, the butterflies in my stomach just couldn't settle! The HEA couldn't be more beautiful if an enhancing spell had been cast, although, Ms Morgan must possess loads of magic within her to make me devour every book she writes! Loved it? Heck no! I ADORED this book! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A194A75Y5I1DW2\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":1,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:25833456":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":25833456,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1717178978i/25833456._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":53,"textReviewsCount":213,"name":"Michelle","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/25833456-michelle","contributor":null,"id":25833456},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A16P6MRVCDSJ9C":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A16P6MRVCDSJ9C"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A16P6MRVCDSJ9C\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A16P6MRVCDSJ9C","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A16P6MRVCDSJ9C"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25833456?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"fantasy-sci-fi","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25833456?shelf=fantasy-sci-fi"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"favorites","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/25833456?shelf=favorites"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8600190496"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.T9vSYsv2F80fLpfW34moyg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.T9vSYsv2F80fLpfW34moyg","creator":{"__ref":"User:25833456"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778743249114,"createdAt":1778741823648,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1778743248954,"text":"This was so cute I just about had a giggle fit over it. I adore the chemistry between Bastian and Aveline so much. Rachel Morgan is extremely talented at crafting characters that feel very well realized, with insecurities and hang ups that are poignant and feel extremely relatable. All 4 of these Charmed Leaf Legacy books I have read have left me feeling seen in some capacity - each character has something they struggle with, and it always strikes a chord for me. This story - a novella really - strikes the nail on the head again. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFrost \u0026amp; Fae Bargains is a forced proximity romance following side characters that are briefly mentioned in the main series, Aveline Thornhart and Bastian Blackbriar. Their story is our first non-Rowanwood romance set within this world, and it’s just as good as the main series. Morgan does a great job at fleshing out the winter traditions of the higher echelons of Fae Society, and crafts a delightfully cozy winter read that glitters like snow. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI really appreciate how Bastian and Aveline’s struggles are very nearly mirrors of each other: he, the disappointing second son who is never good enough, and Aveline, who is made to stifle her real personality as much as possible. Both of them hide behinds facades, and it is the slow melting of their masks that makes this story so well plotted and engaging to read. You truly end up rooting for both of them, because it is so clear that they are drawn to each other like magnets because of how much they are kindred spirits. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSomething I have appreciated about this series is how extremely character driven it is, owing to the fact that there is never real high stakes. It’s a cozy regency inspired setting, and as such the characters have to be the driving force for the narrative to be engaging. This is Rachel Morgan’s greatest strength. Her dialogue craft is excellent - she’s very good with banter and chemistry and it’s something I always look forward to with this series. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThat said, something I would like to see with the remaining Charmed Leaf Legacy titles we are to receive later this year is perhaps a little bit more world building. I adore this series; I have loved every single title I have read within it. I want to know more about this world we get snatched glimpses of more and more with every book, so I am hoping Kazrian and Rosavyn’s stories deliver in this regard. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis series has shaped up to be one of my favorite indie series I have read, and I highly recommend it for those readers who want a change of pace with a swoony-not-spicy romance. ","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A16P6MRVCDSJ9C\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:173989381":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":173989381,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1710213501i/173989381._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":7,"textReviewsCount":164,"name":"Brittany Rolph","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/173989381-brittany-rolph","contributor":null,"id":173989381},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AF8OF014KN83":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AF8OF014KN83"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AF8OF014KN83\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AF8OF014KN83","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AF8OF014KN83"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/173989381?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8576077935"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.cIj1WP9Bl-4XxE3hjVTklg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.cIj1WP9Bl-4XxE3hjVTklg","creator":{"__ref":"User:173989381"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1777940773538,"createdAt":1777940025833,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1777940773329,"text":"Oh my goodness, another winner for Rachel. The love I have for the series is SO much. I love the world and the characters she’s created. This was such a fun surprise book \u0026amp; I loved going back in time a bit and seeing some of our beloved characters before they met their match. 🥹 \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI was captivated quickly by the story between Bastian \u0026amp; Aveline. Rachel once again writes the most delicious tension and swoon that will give you one million butterflies and you’ll be soaking up every single moment! I was giggling and kicking my feet over subtle looks \u0026amp; hand brushes 🤭\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBastian has this carefree attitude about him, but you could also tell very quickly that there was more beneath it. Aveline was the most prim \u0026amp; proper, until she met Bastian and slipped and showed her true colors (pun intended!), which intrigued Bastian! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe story woven throughout this was filled with hope \u0026amp; accepting who you are and being yourself wholly \u0026amp; completely. Bastian saw through the facade that Aveline had up and saw her tenacity \u0026amp; competitive side, and he often pushed her to show that side of herself. He showed her there was nothing wrong with who she was. I loved watching him help her believe it! And how he helped her with her magic?! Doing it anytime she needed \u0026amp; doing it without even thinking. He was just always aware of her needs, and always listening.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd she did the same for Bastian. He often felt second best, but she showed him he wasn’t. That he had just as much to offer as any other eligible man. That his magic wasn’t just to boast others up, that it could truly help others! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd Aveline’s Magic?! It sounded so beautiful. I could picture it so vividly in my head. I felt like I was transported to another world as she’d describe it! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOk this is the longest review ever, but I just loved this book SO much!! \u003cbr /\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AF8OF014KN83\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:44389852":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":44389852,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1546289293i/44389852._UY200_CR33,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":13,"textReviewsCount":150,"name":"Mariette De kock","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/44389852-mariette-de-kock","contributor":null,"id":44389852},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2R5WY5HSR571J":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2R5WY5HSR571J"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2R5WY5HSR571J\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2R5WY5HSR571J","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2R5WY5HSR571J"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/44389852?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"2026-reads","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/44389852?shelf=2026-reads"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"e-kindle-own","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/44389852?shelf=e-kindle-own"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"star-5","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/44389852?shelf=star-5"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8575363577"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ODWaLA8Ns3dOGMQ4zlJnNg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ODWaLA8Ns3dOGMQ4zlJnNg","creator":{"__ref":"User:44389852"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778699988183,"createdAt":1778699863466,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1778699988006,"text":"Frost \u0026amp; Fae Bargains by Rachel Morgan\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e📚Bonus book in The Charmed Leaf Legacy series \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e🎨️ Regency-inspired setting\u003cbr /\u003e🩵Fake courtship\u003cbr /\u003e🎨️️Forced proximity\u003cbr /\u003e🩵He falls first\u003cbr /\u003e🎨️️ Bonus book\u003cbr /\u003e🩵 light, cozy fantasy\u003cbr /\u003e🎨️️ swoony, no-spice romance\u003cbr /\u003e🩵 standalone\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe book follows Lady Aveline Thornhart and Lord Bastian Blackbriar as they both attend the Rowanwood Midwinter Revels. Ava’s grandmother wants her to be on her best and most ladylike behaviour, especially after last Bloom season’s magical display ended in a disaster. Bastion’s mother is trying to get him to settle and give their family a better magical position in society. She thinks Lady Ava will make the perfect wife. Ave is on her best behaviour and Bastian is doing everything to sabotage the courtship. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis is a close door romantasy (Romance \u0026amp; fantasy) with fae, magic and banter. It is describe as “A Cozy Fantasy Romance”. This couldn’t be more true! I absolutely loved this story. I loved everything about it. The fashion, the courtships, the traditions and the romance.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe charmed leaf series is a favourite and this book is an excellent edition. It's so easy and intriguing that I read it in a day. The atmosphere is magically and mystically. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAve and Bastian story is everything you want in a book. Enemies to friends to lovers , the banter and forced proximity . Bastion brings out the best of Ava. He helps her in more way than one. Ava sees past Bastion’s performance and see the real him. They are perfect for each other.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIt is amazing to have a smut free series that doesn’t end on a cliffhanger. Rachel Morgan’s writing is amazing and so far I have loved all her books that I have read. I can’t wait to continue the series.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e#Reading #bookstagrammer#review #southafricanauthor #kindle","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2R5WY5HSR571J\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:168466507":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":168466507,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1785463589i/168466507._UY200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":0,"textReviewsCount":65,"name":"Ashten Ferguson","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/168466507-ashten-ferguson","contributor":null,"id":168466507},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AWK0F2MYN0EFQ":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AWK0F2MYN0EFQ"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AWK0F2MYN0EFQ\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AWK0F2MYN0EFQ","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AWK0F2MYN0EFQ"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/168466507?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8653806492"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.-XkgvaxSUTXU8391mkfx4A":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.-XkgvaxSUTXU8391mkfx4A","creator":{"__ref":"User:168466507"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1780427776980,"createdAt":1780427759451,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1780427776805,"text":"REVIEW TIME: ⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️, \"Frost \u0026amp; Fae Bargains\" by @authorrachelmorgan ! The most recent in the world of the Charmed Leaf Legacy series (but time wise set right before book one Temptests and Tea Leaves.) It was a grand time just like all the books leading up to this one! I loved the whimsical christmas festivities vibe in this one... very cozy and lots of vivid detail/a fun read! This one spoke to me personally as I have struggles similar to both the FMC and MMC in feeling either not enough or too much simultaneously. There was a little side kick frost faerie in the story and she is spunky, hilarious, attentive, and everything a fun side kick should be! I love that the book ended with the FMC and her grandmother finding mutual ground and healing in thier differences. As always the romance was divine. We start out as mutual enemies to lovers turned partners in crime driving each other mad but by the end they are full of yearning, swoon worthy pining, and sweet touches of affection/kisses only. A 1 on my SPICE SCALE🌶️, because while there was absolutely 0 spice or language, there is detailed descriptions (in the end of the book in one scene) of desire and what it's making them feel. Rachel has done it again!! **To read this free copy latest installment of The Charmed Leaf series, go to Rachel's website now and sign up for her newsletter! She'll send you an email with links to all her bonus content as this is a standalone bonus story. ** #charmedleafseries #faeregencyromantasy #rachelmorganreads #whimsicalwinterreads #frostandfaebargains happy reading!! LINK: \u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" href=\"https://join.rachel-morgan.com/frost\"\u003ehttps://join.rachel-morgan.com/frost\u003c/a\u003e","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AWK0F2MYN0EFQ\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:192911929":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":192911929,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1757440291i/192911929._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":0,"textReviewsCount":87,"name":"Ulrike","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/192911929-ulrike","contributor":null,"id":192911929},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2UZPZKN2DUJ00":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2UZPZKN2DUJ00"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2UZPZKN2DUJ00\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2UZPZKN2DUJ00","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2UZPZKN2DUJ00"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/192911929?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/8707245068"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2026062215.1b01eb0f-63c0-4197-92b5-2bfaf7cf43a0":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v2.2026062215.1b01eb0f-63c0-4197-92b5-2bfaf7cf43a0","creator":{"__ref":"User:192911929"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1782141796840,"createdAt":1782141755551,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1782141796684,"text":"She is expected to suppress her creative magic and present herself as the perfect lady in order to attract a respectable suitor. He, in turn, is supposed to court her—yet he seems far more interested in teasing her and drawing her out of her shell. When Bastian Blackbriar and Lady Aveline Thornhart meet during the twelve-day Midwinter celebration at the Rowanwood family's country estate, sparks and misunderstandings are inevitable.\u003cbr /\u003eTo escape the scrutiny of their relatives, they agree to pretend an interest in one another. But the more time they spend together, the more genuine their feelings become.\u003cbr /\u003eWitty banter, lovable and eccentric characters, and moments filled with honesty, joy, and warmth make this a thoroughly enjoyable read. I especially loved the way Bastian and Aveline truly see one another and offer each other support and encouragement. While I appreciated the fact that everything works out in the end, the resolution felt a little too neat and idealised to be entirely believable.\u003cbr /\u003eAll in all, Frost \u0026amp; Fae Bargains is a charming cosy fantasy romance that is light, entertaining, and easy to enjoy.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2UZPZKN2DUJ00\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.id60MM8QrttxTJre\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:161300758":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":161300758,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1699972311i/161300